WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.275
Unit 2 is the guide's Step 8.

2
00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:06.306
Managed identities themselves are
covered in the service account guide;

3
00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.288
this step covers the vault they read.

4
00:00:08.288 --> 00:00:13.000
Create vaults on role-based access with
purge protection, and close the firewall,

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.587
with the commands from Learn's
Private Link integration page.

6
00:00:16.587 --> 00:00:19.562
Purge protection can't be
turned off once it's on;

7
00:00:19.562 --> 00:00:23.300
that's the point, and the guide
never excludes a vault from it.

8
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.896
Grant the workload's managed
identity a data-plane role,

9
00:00:26.896 --> 00:00:31.587
such as Key Vault Secrets User, at the
vault's scope, not the subscription's.

10
00:00:31.587 --> 00:00:36.212
Administrators get Key Vault Administrator
as an eligible pim assignment.

11
00:00:36.212 --> 00:00:41.672
Rotate keys by policy, with Learn's autorotation
command; the periods in the guide's

12
00:00:41.672 --> 00:00:46.650
policy file are an example, and the
agency's key management policy sets them.

13
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.820
And send the audit event
log to the workspace,

14
00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.075
as Learn's page, Enable
Key Vault logging, shows.

15
00:00:53.075 --> 00:00:57.740
Learn also recommends one vault per
application, region and environment.
